          "recommended_because": "The rule closes the project-finance gap on its face and reopens it through the definition; stated flatly that is the point.",
          "text": "This commitment appears to close the gap its neighbour leaves open. It reaches “other direct financing”, not only project finance.\n\nThe definition decides how far. Direct financing is financing “where the use of proceeds is known to be for a particular project”. A general corporate facility, a revolving credit line or a bond with no stated use is not direct financing, so it is not restricted, whatever the energy group spends it on.\n\nAnd only energy groups are covered: groups with over 20% of revenue from upstream oil and gas, and the majors. Expansion counts only for projects sanctioned after 2021.\n\nWhat remains is earmarked financing for a new project, which a producer with a choice need not ask for."
